  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a permanent 7% no-sale ceiling (not 5%), with a 5% corrective-action trigger, so Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10 is not barred from sale; per-model results are withheld from the public but disclosed to purchasers under S2/S5 wording. S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000 per model with no transition, which would hit Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S4 suppression at 36 months sits within the acceptable range and S3 retrofit at 6 years protects Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. Caveat: S2 does not explicitly say customers receive numeric rates; I coded 'numeric_rates' from S5's 'latest 55 °C sustained-heat test results' wording, which is ambiguous. S3 new-unit deadline of 24 months is outside the acceptable 12-month bound."
